C:Trefniant Meurig Williams
H:Known simply as Cambro Brython. Alawon Cymru has it in a set between Mantell Siani and Dic y Cymro: Cambro Brython and Dic y Cymro are often played together in north-east Wales, and the Kilbride brothers are credited with first putting them together. Alawon Cymru's Moliannwn set has it as a square dance, with the second time through part B ending with the second half of part A. In Blodau'r Grug (vol. 3) it's the last of three tunes for the set dance The Cambro Britons (Cambro Brython 1, 2 and 3).
